# React + TypeScript Best Practices for AgileSpace

## Component Structure

Define props with interfaces/types, not prop-types:

```tsx
interface SessionCardProps {
  session: Session;
  onEndSession?: (sessionId: string) => void;
  onEditSession?: (session: Session) => void;
}

export function SessionCard({
  session,
  onEndSession,
  onEditSession,
}: SessionCardProps) {
  return (
    <Card>
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>{session.title}</CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

## Component Declaration

Use the function keyword for components:

```tsx
// ✅ Good
export function SpaceSidebar({ space }: SpaceSidebarProps) {
  return <div>...</div>;
}

// ❌ Avoid
export const SpaceSidebar = ({ space }: SpaceSidebarProps) => {
  return <div>...</div>;
};
```

## Hooks Usage

- Call hooks only at the top level of components
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks with `use-*` prefix
- Use `use-*-api` prefix for data fetching hooks

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Custom hooks
export function useSessions(spaceId: string) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ["sessions", spaceId],
    queryFn: () => getSessions(spaceId),
  });
}

// ✅ Good - API hooks
export function useSessionsApi(spaceId: string) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ["sessions", spaceId],
    queryFn: () =>
      supabase.from("sessions").select("*").eq("space_id", spaceId),
  });
}
```

## Performance Optimization

- Memoize with React.memo, useCallback, useMemo where appropriate
- Avoid inline functions in JSX—pull handlers out or wrap in useCallback
- Use React.lazy + Suspense for code splitting

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Memoized component
export const SessionList = React.memo(function SessionList({
  sessions,
}: SessionListProps) {
  return (
    <div>
      {sessions.map((session) => (
        <SessionCard key={session.id} session={session} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
});

// ✅ Good - Memoized callback
const handleEndSession = useCallback(
  (sessionId: string) => {
    endSessionMutation.mutate(sessionId);
  },
  [endSessionMutation]
);
```

## Composition Patterns

- Favor composition (render props, children) over inheritance
- Use Radix UI components for consistent design system
- Leverage TanStack Query for data fetching and caching

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Composition with children
export function Card({ children, className }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <div
      className={cn(
        "rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground shadow-sm",
        className
      )}
    >
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Error Handling

- Implement error boundaries for component error handling
- Use TanStack Query error states for API errors
- Provide clear, user-friendly error messages

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Error boundary
export function ErrorBoundary({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <ErrorBoundary fallback={<div>Something went wrong</div>}>
      {children}
    </ErrorBoundary>
  );
}

// ✅ Good - Query error handling
const { data, error, isLoading } = useSessionsApi(spaceId);

if (error) {
  return <div>Failed to load sessions: {error.message}</div>;
}
```

## Form Handling

- Use react-hook-form with zod validation
- Prefer controlled components for forms
- Separate client-side and server-side validation

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Form with validation
const form = useForm<SessionFormData>({
  resolver: zodResolver(sessionSchema),
  defaultValues: {
    title: "",
    description: "",
  },
});
```

## Cleanup and Effects

- Clean up effects in useEffect to prevent leaks
- Use guard clauses (early returns) for error handling
- Handle loading states properly

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Effect with cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  const interval = setInterval(() => {
    updateTimer();
  }, 1000);

  return () => clearInterval(interval);
}, [updateTimer]);
```

## File Organization

- Export components as named exports
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Use descriptive names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)
- File layout: exported component → subcomponents → hooks/helpers → static content
